    "body": "An AI-friendly iOS/iPadOS automation service. Tell your agent *\"My iPhone is running iCTRL at <ip>:8200 — figure out how to drive it.\"* and it reads the on-device manual and takes it from there. Works with any agent that can make HTTP requests: OpenClaw, Hermes, Minis, Claude Code, Codex and others.\n\n## Downloads\n\n### Which IPA do I need?\n\n| File | Needed? | What it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `iCTRLUITests-Runner.ipa` | **Required** | The automation engine. It serves the JSON-RPC API that agents and clients call, and must be running. |\n| `iCTRL.ipa` | Optional | A companion app for tasks on the phone itself: <br>• mount the Developer Disk Image without a Mac, and remount it after a reboot <br>• start and stop the runner <br>• choose who can reach the runner (this device only / LAN / LAN + nearby) <br>• see and revoke authorized clients <br>• read the runner's log live |\n\nSkip `iCTRL.ipa` if you mount the Developer Disk Image with Xcode or StikDebug, and manage the runner from its notification or a computer. With a free Apple ID you get three sideloaded apps, and SideStore uses one of them. Install StikDebug *or* the iCTRL app alongside the runner, not both.\n\nBoth IPAs are unsigned for distribution (ad-hoc, no provisioning profile). Sign them when you install:\n- **Free Apple ID:** the latest SideStore signs and installs them. Older SideStore releases skip the nested `.xctest`, and the runner then crashes on launch.\n- **Paid account:** `Scripts/sign-ipa.sh -i iCTRLUITests-Runner.ipa`\n\nThe runner also needs the Developer Disk Image mounted (Xcode, StikDebug or the iCTRL app). The [README](https://github.com/OpenMinis/iCTRL#installation) covers the whole setup.\n\n## What's new since 1.98.15\n\n### Input\n- **Continuous single-finger drag paths.** `drag` accepts a `points` array (2-64 waypoints, 0.1-10 s) and follows it with one finger, pressing once and lifting once. Draw corners, unlock patterns, drag-to-reorder. Corners can be rounded by 1-2 pt, so keep each segment at least one frame long. Advertised as the `drag_path` capability. Existing endpoint/ref drags are unchanged. Thanks to @YanYunNN.\n\n### Build\n- `make ipa UNSIGNED=1` builds release IPAs without a signing identity.\n\n## Earlier in 1.98.13 - 1.98.15\n- The video stream skips identical frames while the screen is still, and no longer goes black after the runner was in the background.\n- The remote page keeps FPS, quality and verbose across reloads.\n- `type` falls back to on-screen key taps when a field drops focus and reports failures. `keyboard.visible` detects third-party keyboards.\n- More methods require authorization. The iCTRL app imports RemotePairing files such as StikDebug's pairingFile.plist.\n",
